The relevant rules are those about inheritance of east‑west relations from containers to their contents and about transitive west/east relations.  
Box 1 is east of Box 3, and Box 3 is east of Box 2, so Box 2 is west of Box 3 and Box 3 is west of Box 1. No rule allows us to conclude that Box 2 (and thus the orange apple inside it) is west of Box 1. Therefore we cannot assert that the medium orange apple is west of Box 1, so the statement “all medium orange apples are west of box one” is false.

